verify_outputs	Compare requested and applied safe outputs	2026-10-21T18:24:30.5112385Z   AGENT_OUTPUT: {"items":[{"type":"add_labels","labels":["C: parser"]},{"type":"add_comment","body":"Thanks for the report! This is an automated first-pass triage; a maintainer will make the final call.\n\n**Reproduction:** Black 26.3.0, default flags, using the `lazy import random` snippet: parse error (`Cannot parse: 1:5: lazy import random`). This matches your console output.\n**Assessment:** This looks like a valid feature request. The `lazy` soft keyword from PEP 810 (Python 3.15) isn't in Black's grammar yet, so any file using it fails to parse. The style docs in this repository don't mention it. I labelled it `C: parser` because the change would be in the vendored parser (blib2to3).\n**Next step:** A maintainer will need to decide whether to add `lazy` import support now, while 3.15 is still in alpha, or wait for the grammar to stabilise. The PEP is at https://peps.python.org/pep-0810/.\n\n<sub>black-issue-triage skill v1.0.0 · suggested for maintainers: none</sub>","temporary_id":"aw_8ikq24Dk"}],"errors":[]}
